{"t": 1793686076.758544, "s": 0.38, "code": "import numpy as np\nnp.set_printoptions(precision=4, suppress=True, linewidth=160)\nprint(\"shapes:\")\nfor k in sorted(W):\n    print(k, W[k].shape)\nprint(\"\\nLN weights stats:\")\nfor l in range(4):\n    for nm in [f\"ln1_w.{l}\",f\"ln1_b.{l}\",f\"ln2_w.{l}\",f\"ln2_b.{l}\"]:\n        a=W[nm]\n        print(nm, \"mean\",a.mean(),\"std\",a.std(),\"min\",a.min(),\"max\",a.max(),\"norm\",np.linalg.norm(a))\nfor nm in [\"lnf_w\",\"lnf_b\"]:\n    if nm in W:\n        a=W[nm]; print(nm, a.shape, a.mean(),a.std(),a.min(),a.max(),np.linalg.norm(a))\nprint(\"\\nLayer/head norms and singular values:\")\nfor l in range(4):\n    print(\"LAYER\",l)\n    # overall\n    for name in [\"W_q\",\"W_k\",\"W_v\",\"W_o\",\"W_fc\",\"W_proj\"]:\n        a=W[f\"{name}.{l}\"]\n        print(name, \"shape\",a.shape,\"norm\",np.linalg.norm(a),\"mean\",a.mean(),\"std\",a.std())\n    for j in range(6):\n        s=slice(j*64,(j+1)*64)\n        wq=W[f\"W_q.{l}\"][s,:]; wk=W[f\"W_k.{l}\"][s,:]; wv=W[f\"W_v.{l}\"][s,:]\n        wo=W[f\"W_o.{l}\"][:,s]  # in x out? W_o is 384x384, columns head segment\n        # singular vals\n        sq=np.linalg.svd(wq, compute_uv=False); sk=np.linalg.svd(wk, compute_uv=False); sv=np.linalg.svd(wv, compute_uv=False); so=np.linalg.svd(wo, compute_uv=False)\n        # bilinear QK matrix Wq @ Wk.T, out x out\n        A=wq@wk.T\n        sa=np.linalg.svd(A, compute_uv=False)\n        # OV = Wo[:,s] @ Wv? Actually output contribution = att @ v @ W_o^T, head v = h W_v^T; out = att @ h W_v^T W_o[:,s].T? Effective OV from residual input to output: W_v^T? shapes: wv=64x384, wo=384x64, product wv? for each token: v = h @ wv.T (n x64); out = v @ wo.T? code out[:,s] = att @ v[:,s]; then x += out @ W_o.T. out whole n x384, W_o.T 384x384? Wait W_o.l is 384x384, out @ W_o.T. For columns s of out (dims residual?), W_o.T rows dims s? Actually out[:,s] active dims j*hd..; multiplied by W_o.T, where rows of W_o.T correspond dims? out (n,384) @ W_o.T (384,384): contribution to residual = sum_d out[:,d] W_o[:,d]? W_o.T[d, outdim]=W_o[outdim,d]. So columns of W_o correspond input head dims d. Thus effective map input residual h -> v -> output = h @ wv.T @ wo.T? v (n,64)=h (n,384) @ wv.T (384,64). contribution = v @ wo.T (64,384) where wo = W_o[:,s] (384,64). So effective = wv.T @ wo.T? h @ wv.T @ wo.T = h @ (wo @ wv).T? Check (wv.T @ wo.T) shape 384x384. Its rank <=64. Effective output = h @ (wv.T @ wo.T). Equiv h @ (wo @ wv).T? (wo@wv) shape 384x384, transpose same. Wait (wv.T @ wo.T) = (wo @ wv).T. So OV matrix maybe wo @ wv. We'll compute singular values of wo@wv (384x384).\n        OV = wo @ wv  # output x input (resid_out = h @ OV.T?) rank 64\n        sov=np.linalg.svd(OV, compute_uv=False)\n        # QK bilinear can be Wq @ Wk.T -> x Wq^T Wk x'^T? score q k^T = (x wq.T)(x' wk.T)^T = x wq.T wk x'^T. matrix wq.T wk (384x384)\n        QK = wq.T @ wk  # input x input\n        sqk=np.linalg.svd(QK, compute_uv=False)\n        print(f\" H{j}: |q|={np.linalg.norm(wq):.3f} |k|={np.linalg.norm(wk):.3f} |v|={np.linalg.norm(wv):.3f} |o|={np.linalg.norm(wo):.3f} \"\n              f\"svq[0:4]={sq[:4]} svk[0:4]={sk[:4]} svv[0:4]={sv[:4]} svo[0:4]={so[:4]} \"\n              f\"|A|={np.linalg.norm(A):.3f} svA[0:4]={sa[:4]} svOV[0:4]={sov[:4]} svQK[0:4]={sqk[:4]}\")\n", "out": "shapes:\nW_fc.0 (1536, 384)\nW_fc.1 (1536, 384)\nW_fc.2 (1536, 384)\nW_fc.3 (1536, 384)\nW_k.0 (384, 384)\nW_k.1 (384, 384)\nW_k.2 (384, 384)\nW_k.3 (384, 384)\nW_o.0 (384, 384)\nW_o.1 (384, 384)\nW_o.2 (384, 384)\nW_o.3 (384, 384)\nW_proj.0 (384, 1536)\nW_proj.1 (384, 1536)\nW_proj.2 (384, 1536)\nW_proj.3 (384, 1536)\nW_q.0 (384, 384)\nW_q.1 (384, 384)\nW_q.2 (384, 384)\nW_q.3 (384, 384)\nW_v.0 (384, 384)\nW_v.1 (384, 384)\nW_v.2 (384, 384)\nW_v.3 (384, 384)\nln1_b.0 (384,)\nln1_b.1 (384,)\nln1_b.2 (384,)\nln1_b.3 (384,)\nln1_w.0 (384,)\nln1_w.1 (384,)\nln1_w.2 (384,)\nln1_w.3 (384,)\nln2_b.0 (384,)\nln2_b.1 (384,)\nln2_b.2 (384,)\nln2_b.3 (384,)\nln2_w.0 (384,)\nln2_w.1 (384,)\nln2_w.2 (384,)\nln2_w.3 (384,)\n\nLN weights stats:\nln1_w.0 mean 0.24030669 std 0.24358396 min -0.0010124741 max 1.0340554 norm 6.705139\nln1_b.0 mean 0.0008393097 std 0.028742684 min -0.095908366 max 0.091023624 norm 0.56347936\nln2_w.0 mean 0.80056995 std 0.32951427 min 0.0044303946 max 1.5072498 norm 16.964813\nln2_b.0 mean 0.0021705579 std 0.06830766 min -0.49860355 max 0.33306837 norm 1.339227\nln1_w.1 mean 0.45753345 std 0.10221135 min 0.13610736 max 1.1238989 norm 9.186787\nln1_b.1 mean -0.0050218217 std 0.16716056 min -1.4712496 max 1.1544172 norm 3.2771423\nln2_w.1 mean 1.0428675 std 0.20026265 min -0.0019355153 max 1.4855961 norm 20.80933\nln2_b.1 mean 0.00053805806 std 0.136417 min -0.3596882 max 0.36863092 norm 2.673237\nln1_w.2 mean 0.7052056 std 0.07490397 min 0.20780912 max 1.0144427 norm 13.896884\nln1_b.2 mean -0.0010484305 std 0.15254197 min -1.3819015 max 1.0526733 norm 2.9892702\nln2_w.2 mean 1.3122883 std 0.12551987 min 0.0011308102 max 1.4654561 norm 25.83286\nln2_b.2 mean 0.004968606 std 0.15366812 min -0.3761152 max 0.38859338 norm 3.0128415\nln1_w.3 mean 0.7545757 std 0.054236066 min 0.29438865 max 0.87010384 norm 14.82475\nln1_b.3 mean 0.012112465 std 0.08487788 min -0.6069081 max 0.6501508 norm 1.6801105\nln2_w.3 mean 1.2777737 std 0.08074604 min 0.43639854 max 1.4306335 norm 25.089094\nln2_b.3 mean 0.004284037 std 0.12758872 min -0.67276204 max 0.30676207 norm 2.5016272\n\nLayer/head norms and singular values:\nLAYER 0\nW_q shape (384, 384) norm 32.29116 mean 0.00025943352 std 0.08409116\nW_k shape (384, 384) norm 30.390932 mean -0.00011999023 std 0.07914296\nW_v shape (384, 384) norm 14.836016 mean 5.6603043e-05 std 0.038635418\nW_o shape (384, 384) norm 16.371328 mean -0.00011180931 std 0.042633522\nW_fc shape (1536, 384) norm 46.24861 mean -0.0011808213 std 0.06020797\nW_proj shape (384, 1536) norm 39.307518 mean -5.5428252e-05 std 0.051181637\n H0: |q|=3.305 |k|=4.180 |v|=6.039 |o|=6.666 svq